BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Space Shuttle final approach</h1>
<p>Final approach to SLF runway 33 at the Kennedy Space Center.</p>
<p>Initially pitch down to -15°. Use the PAPI indicators ahead of the runway for glideslope adjustment.
Use the split rudder speed brake (Ctrl-B) to bleed off airspeed.</p>
<p>On approach, slowly raise the nose to touch down with an AOA of approx. +10°.
Lower your gear during the final flare-up, about 10 seconds before touchdown.
Touchdown speed is approximately 100 m/s.</p>
END_HYPERDESC

